# Quote Response Document Generation — MANDATORY TEMPLATE

**When Dee provides a solicitation number, PDF, or says "generate a response" / "bid on this" / "respond to this" — NEXUS generates a multi-page quote response document using this template. Automatically. No extra instructions needed.**

---

## The Trigger

**Any of these inputs from Dee triggers quote response generation:**
- A solicitation number (e.g., "N0017426Q1009")
- A solicitation PDF or text file
- "Generate a response for [solicitation]"
- "Bid on this"
- "Respond to this"
- "Create a quote response"
- Any solicitation dropped into the conversation

**When triggered, NEXUS:**
1. Parses the solicitation (agency, SOW, CLINs, requirements, NAICS, set-aside, evaluation, CO, deadline)
2. Identifies the service lane → looks up colors in `cap-statement-colors.mdc`
3. Copies `GENERATED_RESPONSES/QUOTE_RESPONSE_TEMPLATE.html`
4. Replaces all `{{PLACEHOLDER}}` values with solicitation content
5. Applies ProposalBio to buyer-facing sections (see below)
6. Verifies company info per `company-info-verification.mdc`
7. Saves in `SEND_TO_BUYER/` and tells Dee it's ready

**No asking "should I generate a response?" — if Dee gives you a solicitation, the response is what she wants.**

---

## The Rule

**Every quote/bid response document generated by NEXUS MUST:**
1. Use the template at `GENERATED_RESPONSES/QUOTE_RESPONSE_TEMPLATE.html`
2. Follow the multi-page structure defined in that template
3. Match the color scheme to the capability statement for that bid (same colors, always)
4. Include a Table of Contents on page 2
5. Place each section on its own page using `<div class="content-page">`
6. Apply ProposalBio to all buyer-facing content (Technical, Past Performance, Compliance Matrix)
7. Be saved as a proper HTML file in the bid's `SEND_TO_BUYER/` folder

**A quote response is NOT a capability statement. It is a MULTI-PAGE document.**

---

## ProposalBio in Quote Responses

**The Technical Capability section, Past Performance section, and Compliance Matrix are buyer-facing content. ProposalBio applies to all three.**

| Biohack | How It Applies to Quote Response |
|---|---|
| #1 Mirror Neuron | Match tone to agency type — Federal = formal, State = moderate, Local = conversational |
| #2 Cognitive Ease | 6-8th grade reading level. Short sentences. No jargon walls. White space between sections. |
| #5 Yes Stacking | Every capability bullet mirrors a SOW requirement = mental "yes" from evaluator |
| #6 Familiarity | Use the EXACT terminology from the solicitation — not DDI's words, THEIR words |
| #7 Name Recognition | Agency name appears 3+ times across the document. Reference their mission. |
| #8 Sensory Language | Specific numbers: "rejection rate below 1.8%", "900 scans/year", "48-hour turnaround" |
| #10 Eye Tracking | Scannable layout via tables, bullets, section headers. Evaluator finds answers in 30 seconds. |

**The pricing table, SAM.gov verification, and certifications sections are factual — ProposalBio doesn't apply to data tables, only to narrative content.**

---

## Document Structure (EVERY response follows this)

| Page | Content | Required |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Cover Page** — Logo, company bar, solicitation title, agency, info grid, cert badges, EDWOSB box | ALWAYS |
| 2 | **Table of Contents** — Numbered sections with page references | ALWAYS |
| 3 | **Section 01: Company Information** — Standard DDI info table | ALWAYS |
| 4+ | **Section 02: Technical Capability** — Tailored to solicitation scope | ALWAYS |
| 5+ | **Section 03: Pricing** — CLINs from solicitation, firm fixed prices | ALWAYS |
| 6+ | **Section 04: Past Performance** — Relevant references with contact info | ALWAYS |
| 7+ | **Section 05: SAM.gov Verification** — Standard table | ALWAYS |
| 8+ | **Section 06: Small Business Certifications** — Standard table | ALWAYS |
| 9+ | **Section 07: Compliance Matrix** — Requirement-by-requirement compliance | ALWAYS |

**Additional sections may be added between 02-04 if the solicitation requires them (e.g., Management Approach, Staffing Plan, Quality Control Plan). Adjust TOC page numbers accordingly.**

