## Critical CSS Rules (WHY this template works for PDF)

The template uses these CSS properties to ensure proper page breaks:

```css
@page { size: 8.5in 11in; margin: 0.6in 0.75in; }
.cover { page-break-after: always; }
.toc { page-break-after: always; }
.content-page { page-break-before: always; }
.pricing-table, .compliance-table, .pp-card { page-break-inside: avoid; }
```

**DO NOT modify these properties. They are what makes the multi-page PDF work.**

**DO NOT use `min-height: 92vh` on the cover page.** The template uses `min-height: 9.3in` which is calibrated for letter size.

**DO NOT remove `page-break-before: always` from `.content-page`.** Every section starts a new page. That's the whole point.

